    <GaugingStation location="Balmossie Mill" name="Dighty Water" number="14002">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station gauging a predominantly low-lying catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Cableway removed 1999. Summer weed growth necessitates frequent revisions to the stage-discharge relationship. High flow gaugings up to 29.4 cumecs. Potential backing up from bridge at extreme high flows. All flows contained. Multiple peak flow ratings across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity Area station 9m wide. Station added to peak flows dataset in August 2024 (WINFAP Files v13).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Peak flows held from 2008 pending consolidation of earlier ratings.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Very flashy.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Gently sloping and low-lying catchment except for the far N and W edges which drain S flank of Sidlaw Hills (up to 450m). Bedrock predominantly Devonian S'st, mostly overlain by superficial deposits. Lower part of catchment urban (Dundee), the rest mainly arable, with grassland and some forest.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">SI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Rating supported by gaugings to QMED, all flows contained." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Possible backing up at extreme high flows, therefore further work required to be confident of flows greater than QMED." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
